{"title": "Components/Upload/File Upload", "docs": {"text": "FileUpload\nAccessibility Pending\nWeb\nAndroid\niOS\nFlutter\nCMP\n\nFilename\n50%\n60 KB of 12O KB\n\nShow code\nCopy code\nODSFileUpload extends the native HTMLDivElement properties as React props. On top of the additional properties that are listed below, you can also pass the native HTMLDivElement properties as React props. You can read more about those properties here.\n\n\nName\tDescription\tDefault\tControl\nsubtle\t\nDefines the background of the component.\nboolean\ntrue\nFalseTrue\nshowThumbnail\t\nShows/Hides the thumbnail.\nboolean\ntrue\nFalseTrue\nthumbnailProps\t\nDefines the properties of the icon thumbnail.\nODSThumbnailProps\n-\t\n\nthumbnailProps :{\ntype : \"image\"\nimgProps :{...} 2 keys\n}\nbuttonProps\t\nDefines the properties of the action Button.\nODSButtonProps\n-\tSet object\nactionButtonProps\t\nDefines the properties of the action Button.\nODSButtonProps\n-\t\n\nactionButtonProps :{\nbuttonIcon :{...} 5 keys\n}\ntype\t\nDefines the type of the component.\n\"extended\"\n\"simple\"\n\"simple\"\ntype\n\nextended\n\nsimple\nprogressBarProps\t\nDefines the properties of the progressBar. Only use this if you have selected type extended.\nODSProgressBarProps\n-\t\n\nprogressBarProps :{\ncounterText : \"50%\"\nhelperText : \"60 KB of 12O KB\"\nlabelText : \"Filename\"\nprogress : 50\n}\nloading\t\nShows/Hides the loading spinner. Only use this if you have selected type simple.\nboolean\nfalse\nFalseTrue\nlabel\t\nDefines the label of the component.Only use this if you have selected type simple.\nstring\n-\t\n\nGeneral information\n\nFile upload enables users to select and submit files to a designated location, such as an application server or cloud storage. They can support single or multiple uploads and drag-and-drop interactions, while also enforcing rules like file size and type restrictions.\n\nWhen to use\n\nUsers need to provide documents, images, or media as part of a workflow (e.g., profile photos, resumes, receipts).\nFile-based input is essential and cannot be replaced by text, form fields, or structured data entry.\nMultiple files or large file types need to be collected efficiently.\nUsers benefit from previews, progress indicators, or drag-and-drop functionality to simplify the process.\nWhen not to use\n\nThe same information can be entered as text or selected from predefined options (e.g., entering a name vs. uploading a form).\nFiles already exist in the system and can be referenced or reused instead of re-uploaded.\nUploading increases complexity without adding value (e.g., requiring images when a short description would suffice).\nAnatomy\n\n\nUse Directives\n\nFile upload types\n\nExtended\n\nUse this type when you want to display more detailed information by utilizing the progress bar nested inside.\n\n\nSimple\n\nUse this type when you want to display a quick preview with minimum information.\n\n\nShow thumbnail\n\nA thumbnail in a file upload component can hold filetype thumbnails, for example, representing different file formats visually for quick identification.\n\n\nBehaviours\n\nUpload states\n\nThe button is not tied up to the uploading states of the progress bar for full flexibility. You can customise the button to align with the products needs. Following there are a few suggestions of how this would work.\n\nUploading\n\nThe button icon is set to Cancel and it will cancel the upload before completion.\n\n\nUpload completed\n\nThe button icon is set to Delete and it will remove the file from the list.\n\n\nUpload failed\n\nThe button icon is set to Restart and it will attempt the upload again.\n\n\nComponent Variants\n\nType\n\nExtended\n\n\nSimple\n\n\nColour Schemes\n\nWhite\n\n\nBlack\n\n\nMagenta\n\nUse this component only with neutral colour schemes.\n\n\nSecondary\n\nUse this component only with neutral colour schemes.\n\n\nExamples\n\nDesktop\n\n\nMobile\n\n\nAccessibility\n\nThis OneDS component is compliant with WCAG 2.2 AA standards.\n\nKey considerations for keyboard interactions and screen readers are included. Additionally, all components meet requirements for the contrast ratios.\n\nDesign considerations\n\nFile requirements (accepted formats, maximum size) must be clearly visible before upload to prevent errors and should be announced by the screen reader.\nProvide multiple ways to upload files (button + drag & drop) without making drag & drop the only option.\nEnsure the upload area is visually distinct and clearly recognizable as interactive.\nEnsure to announce (visually and by the screen reader) when the upload is finished with success (e.g. \"upload completed\", \"upload 100%\") or with errors.\nBe sure to adapt labels and instructions to the context.\nUpload progress bars will use the same considerations of the Progress Bar component.\nDevelopment considerations\n\nAssociate the file input with a visible label using <label for> or aria-labelledby.\nThe upload container may use role=\"region\" with a descriptive aria-label (e.g. \u201cDocument upload\u201d) to help screen reader users orient themselves.\nKeyboard and screen reader users must be able to upload files using the button.\nWhen files are added, ensure the file list updates are announced appropriately using aria-live=\"polite\" region to announce meaningful changes (e.g. \u201cFile added\u201d, \u201cUpload complete\u201d, \u201cUpload failed\u201d).\nIf thumbnails are shown, mark them decorative (alt=\"\") unless they convey meaningful information\nWhile this individual component is accessible, building fully usable interfaces requires further attention. For guidance, refer to our OneExperience accessibility resources.\n\n", "code": [""], "stories": [{"id": "story--components-fileupload--example-story", "html": "<div id=\"story--components-fileupload--example-story-inner\" data-name=\"Example Story\" lang=\"en\"><div><div style=\"width: 600px; display: flex; padding: 4px;\"><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSFileUpload ODSFileUpload--subtle\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSFileUpload-UploadContent\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSFileUpload-IconProgress\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSThumbnail ODSThumbnail--type-image\"><img alt=\"Profile Image\" class=\"ODSThumbnail-Image ODSThumbnail-Image--type-image\" src=\"https://ods.trap.ng.telekom.net/assets/avatar-profile-BHCvDehJ.png\"></div><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSProgressBar\" aria-disabled=\"false\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSProgressBar-Data\"><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSProgressBar-MainData\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSProgressBar-MainDataText\"><label id=\"_r_14_\" class=\"ODSProgressBar-LabelText ODSProgressBar-LabelText--mode-standard\">Filename</label><span class=\"ODSProgressBar-CounterText ODSProgressBar-CounterText--mode-standard\">50%</span></div><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSProgressBar-DataProgressTrackContainer\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSDataProgressTrack ODSDataProgressTrack--mode-standard ODSDataProgressTrack--size-small ODSDataProgressTrack--progress-25\"><div class=\"ODSBox ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorStart ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorStart--mode-standard ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorStart--progress-25\"></div><div aria-labelledby=\"_r_14_\" role=\"progressbar\" aria-valuemin=\"0\" aria-valuemax=\"100\" aria-valuenow=\"50\" aria-valuetext=\"50%\" class=\"ODSDataProgressTrack-Progress ODSDataProgressTrack-Progress--size-small ODSDataProgressTrack-Progress--mode-standard ODSDataProgressTrack-Progress--progress-25\" style=\"width: 50%;\"></div><div class=\"ODSBox ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorEnd ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorEnd--mode-standard ODSDataProgressTrack-IndicatorEnd--progress-25\"></div></div></div></div></div><span class=\"ODSProgressBar-HelperText ODSProgressBar-HelperText--mode-standard\">60 KB of 12O KB</span></div></div><button class=\"ODSRow ODSButton ODSButton--size-small ODSButton--buttonType-iconOnly ODSButton--variant-ghost ODSButton-ButtonBg--variant-ghost ODSButton-ButtonBg ODSButton-ButtonBg--buttonType-iconOnly 